Implementing a multi-treelist (also known as a tree list or tree grid) within an Angular application can be achieved using the `MatTreeGrid` component from Material Design. Below is a basic example of how you might structure your project and use this component.

### Step 1: Set Up Your Angular Project

If you haven't already set up an Angular project, create one using the following command:

```bash
ng new my-text-editor-app
cd my-text-editor-app
```

### Step 2: Install Material Components

Add the necessary Material components for TreeGrid support:

```bash
npm install @angular/material @ag-grid-enterprise/core --save
```

Then import them into your app module:

```typescript
import { MatTreeGridModule } from '@angular/material/tree-grid';

@NgModule({
  imports: [
    // other modules...
    MatTreeGridModule
  ],
  declarations: [AppComponent],
  bootstrap: [AppComponent]
})
export class AppModule {}
```

### Step 3: Create Data Models

Create data models for your items that will populate the TreeGrid. For simplicity, let's assume we have two types of nodes: "Items" and "Categories".

#### Category Node Model

```typescript
export interface Category {
  id: number;
  name: string;
}
```

#### Item Node Model

```typescript
export interface Item extends Category {
  children?: Item[];
}
```

### Step 4: Implement Multi-Treelist Component

Create a component to display the TreeGrid. Let's call it `MultiTreelistComponent`.

```typescript
import { Component, OnInit } from '@angular/core';
import { MatTreeGridComponent } from '@angular/material/tree-grid';
import { CategoriesService } from './categories.service'; // assuming you have a service for fetching categories

@Component({
  selector: 'app-multi-treelist',
  templateUrl: './multi-treelist.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./multi-treelist.component.css']
})
export class MultiTreelistComponent implements OnInit {
  dataSource = null;

  constructor(private categoryService: CategoriesService) {}

  ngOnInit() {
    this.categoryService.getCategories()
      .subscribe(categories => {
        const rootCategory = { id: 0, name: 'Root' };
        const categoriesData = categories.map(category => ({
          ...category,
          parentCategoryId: -1
        }));
        const expandedRows = categoriesData.filter(c => c.parentCategoryId === -1);
        this.dataSource = {
          columns: [
            { headerName: 'ID', field: 'id', valueGetter: (params: any) => params.data.id },
            { headerName: 'Name', field: 'name', valueGetter: (params: any) => params.data.name }
          ],
          rows: [...expandedRows, ...(categoriesData.filter(row => row.parentCategoryId !== -1))].map(row => ({ rowData: row }))
        };
      });
  }

  onExpand(nodeId) {
    if (nodeId === this.rootNode?.id) return; // Skip root node expansion
    this.categoryService.getSubCategories(nodeId)
      .subscribe(subCategories => {
        const expandedRows = subCategories.map(subCat => ({
          ...subCat,
          parentCategoryId: nodeId
        }));
        this.dataSource.rows = [...this.dataSource.rows, ...expandedRows];
      });
  }
}

```

### Step 5: Update Template

Update the template file (`multi-treelist.component.html`) to render the TreeGrid:

```html
<mat-treegrid #treeGrid>
  <mat-tree-node *matTreeNodeDef="let item">
    <div matTreeNodeIcon>{{item.name}}</div>
    <div matTreeNodeContent>{{item.children?.length || ''}} child

